with our state revealing job numbers for  the state we are now sitting at an  all-time high in employment our state  now has more than 1.4 million jobs which  is 3 000 higher than our previous peak  in 2020 but what does this look like for  those college grads getting jobs  christian has got the details that's  right well college students are  definitely taking advantage of these  work opportunities i spoke to one unlv  student today who says landing a job  after the pandemic was a true blessing  i lived in my family for a while i still  live with their mom and it was  really annoying to not have like any  money to do like anything  nineteen-year-old amani taylor can't  stop smiling underneath her face mask  about her guest service job at unlv  after being unemployed it was really  difficult i applied a bunch of places  got rejected i applied here like months  before i think like a month before i got  accepted and they just happened to text  me and ask if i still wanted the job but  taylor is not alone nevada department of  employment training and rehabilitation's  recent june report states nevada added 7  600 jobs in the past month boosting  employment to more than 90 thousand  since june of 2021. the labor market is  still pretty strong we've had an  experience over the last number of  months where we had  almost twice as many jobs out there as  there were people looking for jobs unlv  professor stephen miller says while the  job market is recovering there is also  restructuring that's happening and  positions to fill although we've now  returned to the prior peak in non-farm  employment  we're still about 35 000 jobs short of  the peak  in leisure and hospitality miller also  says those who quit during the great  resignation left behind opportunities he  says this is ideal for college students  like taylor i would use the handshake  app here keep trying to get the job i  got the job of a miracle i was literally  just applying everywhere and i didn't  have much on my resume  all right if you're looking for work job  recruiters say polish up your resume and  your interview skills referrals and  networking of course can help and  consider internships if possible
 

